Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
This is a minimal bootstrap assembler that runs on the 6502 emulator. It
supports only enough to assemble the next version. It reads input character
by character through memory-mapped I/O and emits raw bytes to output.

- DATA directive: emit raw hex bytes (DATA $XX $XX ...)
- Hex byte constants: 2-digit hex values prefixed with $ (e.g., $0A, $FF)
- Semicolon comments: ; to end of line
- Blank lines and whitespace handling (spaces, tabs)
- Single-pass processing (no labels, no symbols, no program counter tracking)
- Output is a raw binary stream
- Reset vector emitted as final two DATA bytes to set entry point

The assembler processes one directive per line. It skips whitespace, newlines,
and comment lines. When it encounters 'D' (start of DATA), it reads and skips
the remaining "ATA" characters, then parses $XX hex byte values separated by
spaces until end of line.

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
The source is written for the C bootstrap assembler (00/asm.c), which supports:

- DATA $XX: emit hex bytes (2-digit and 4-digit, little-endian for 4-digit)
- DATA "string": emit ASCII string literals with \n escape
- Semicolon comments
- Blank lines

The source uses only DATA with hex bytes. All 6502 instructions are manually
encoded as hex byte sequences. Address calculations are done by hand and
hardcoded. The reset vector at the end points to the entry address $2000.
Comments show the intended 6502 instruction for each DATA line.

